   "rule": {
    "title": "Nouns in -ον",
    "body": "Neuter nouns use the same genitive and dative as λόγος, but nominative and accusative are identical: -ον singular, -α plural. So τὰ ἔργα can be subject or object; let the verb and context decide. A neuter plural subject regularly takes a singular verb.",
    "examples": [
     {
      "gr": "τὰ ἔργα τοῦ θεοῦ",
      "en": "the works of God"
     },
